====Noun====
{{wikidata lexeme|L1266}}
{{en-noun}}

# A [[connection]] between [[place]]s, [[people]], [[event]]s, [[thing]]s, or [[idea]]s.
#: {{ux|en|The mayor’s assistant serves as the '''link''' to the media.}}
#* {{RQ:Cowper Task
|passage=The '''link''' of brotherhood, by which / One common Maker bound me to the kind.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1573|author=w:George Gascoigne|title=A Hundreth Sundry Flowres
|passage= And so by double '''lynkes''' enchaynde themselues in louers life}}
# One element of a [[chain]] or other connected series.
#: {{ux|en|The third '''link''' of the silver chain needs to be resoldered.}}
#: {{ux|en|The weakest '''link'''.}}
# {{abbreviation of|en|hyperlink}}.
#: {{ux|en|The '''link''' on the page points to the sports scores.}}
# {{lb|en|computing}} The connection between [[bus]]es or systems.
#: {{ux|en|A by-N-'''link''' is composed of N lanes.}}
# {{lb|en|mathematics}} One or more [[disjoint]] [[knot]]s, possibly unable to be separated.
# {{lb|en|Sussex}} A thin wild bank of land splitting two cultivated patches and often linking two hills.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Richard John King|title=A Handbook for Travellers in Kent and Sussex|passage=They used formerly to live in caves or huts dug into the side of a bank or "'''link'''," and lined with heath or straw.}}
# {{lb|en|figurative}} An individual person or element in a [[system]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=James O. Young|title=My Sheep Know My Voice: anointed poetry|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=zfDXFn0u4E8C&pg=PA32&dq=%22link%22#v=onepage|page=32|publisher=AuthorHouse
|passage=But know that God is the strongest '''link'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=William Lidwell; Kritina Holden; Jill Butler|title=Universal Principles of Design|location=RockPort|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=3RFyaF7jCZsC&pg=PA262&dq=%22link%22#v=onepage|page=262
|passage=The fuse is the weakest '''link''' in the system. As such, the fuse is also the most valuable '''link''' in the system.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2010|author=Stephen Fairweather|title=The Missing Book of Genesis|pageurl=http://books.google.com/books?id=fwSV0E71YCkC&pg=PA219&dq=%22link%22#v=onepage|page=219|publisher=AuthorHouse
|passage=“{{...}} This is so that nobody can change the way every '''link''' must talk about the formula that I taught to make a real Chain of Universal Love and not a Chain of Love of a group or sect.”}}
# Anything doubled and closed like a link of a chain.
#* {{RQ:Mortimer Husbandry|passage=a '''link''' of horsehair}}
# A [[sausage]] that is not a [[patty]].
# {{lb|en|kinematics}} Any one of the several elementary pieces of a mechanism, such as the fixed frame, or a rod, wheel, mass of confined liquid, etc., by which relative motion of other parts is produced and constrained.
# {{lb|en|engineering}} Any intermediate rod or piece for transmitting force or motion, especially a short connecting rod with a bearing at each end; specifically (in steam engines) the slotted bar, or connecting piece, to the opposite ends of which the eccentric rods are jointed, and by means of which the movement of the valve is varied, in a link motion.
# {{lb|en|surveying}} The length of one joint of Gunter's chain, being the hundredth part of it, or 7.92 inches, the chain being 66 feet in length.
# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[bond]] of [[affinity]], or a [[unit]] of [[valence]] between [[atom]]s; applied to a unit of chemical force or attraction.
# {{lb|en|in the plural}} The windings of a river; the land along a winding stream.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1822|author=[[w:Allan Cunningham (author)|Allan Cunningham]]|chapter=[[s:Traditional Tales of the English and Scottish Peasantry/The King of the Peak|The King of the Peak]]|title=Traditional Tales of the English and Scottish Peasantry|pageurl=https://archive.org/stream/traditionaltales01cunn#page/222/mode/2up|volume=1|page=222
|passage='Dame Foljambe,' said the old man, 'the march of thy tale is like the course of the Wye, seventeen miles of '''links''' and windings down a fair valley five miles long. {{...}}'}}
# {{lb|en|broadcasting}} An [[introductory]] [[cue]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2002|author=Carole Fleming|title=The Radio Handbook|page=53
|passage=Too much talk on a music-based station can cause listeners who tune in for the music to go elsewhere. {{...}} 'Some people will say “your '''link''' has to be 45 seconds long” but I don't do that,' explains the programme controller of Trent FM, Dick Stone.}}

